<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Ban (240)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>ban                                       (list the bans)
ban t &lt;site&gt; [&lt;textfile&gt; [&lt;period&gt;]]      (ban all logins)
ban n &lt;site&gt; [&lt;textfile&gt; [&lt;period&gt;]]      (ban new characters)
ban d &lt;site&gt;                              (lift a ban)
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>ban n *.example.net
ban t 203.0.113.* bantotal.txt 2d 12h
</pre>
<p>Keeps a site, or a group of sites, away from the game. The site may hold 
the wild cards * and&#160;?. A <b>total</b> ban (t) lets no one from the site log 
in, a harsh punishment; a <b>new</b> ban (n) only stops them from making new 
characters.
</p><p>Those who are turned away are shown a text file from the etc directory: 
bantotal.txt for a total ban, bannew.txt for a new-character ban, or the 
file you name. The period, such as 2d 3h 30m (days, hours, minutes), makes 
the ban lift by itself when the time is up. Note that the period comes 
after the text file: to give a period, name the file too.
</p><p>Banning a site that is already banned changes its ban. Bans are kept over 
reboots. The command is logged.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Wizlock</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Users</a>
</pre>




</div>